# anthropic_deployment (Resource)

Manages a scheduled deployment (beta): a configured instance of an agent that binds it to an environment, credentials, initial events, and an optional cron schedule so it can run autonomously. There is no hard-delete endpoint for deployments: destroying this resource always archives it.

`initial_events`, `resources`, and `budget` accept raw JSON matching the API's own request shape, since Terraform-native modeling of their deeply nested unions would dwarf the rest of this schema.

> **API**: `POST/GET/POST/POST/POST/POST /v1/deployments[/{id}][/pause|/unpause|/archive]` (Managed Agents API).
> **Auth**: Standard API key (`api_key` / `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`).
> **Beta header**: `anthropic-beta: managed-agents-2026-04-01`.
> **Cost**: Free for management; sessions triggered by the deployment are billed as usual.

